@title The Demo — Chapter One
@bg road
@mood uneasy

narrate This is a demo chapter. It exists to show every feature the engine has,
so you can copy it and write your own.
narrate A road at dusk. Two people who have not decided whether to trust each other.

@card wanderer
narrate The Wanderer has walked this road for eleven days.

@mood calm
wanderer neutral "You're the Keeper of the hall, then."
keeper neutral "I am."
wanderer warm "I expected someone older."
keeper dry "Everyone does."

narrate The Keeper does not smile, but something near it moves.

@diary people the Wanderer, the Keeper.
@diary places the road, the hall.
@ach first_steps

@mood uneasy
keeper neutral "You came a long way to ask me something. Ask it."
wanderer neutral "I came to ask whether the hall still takes people in."

choice
* "Tell the truth: you have nowhere else."     => truth+1, bonds+1
* "Say nothing and wait."                       => conviction+1
* [Bonds 2] "Say you knew her mother."          => bonds+2, mercy+1
* "Lie. Say you were sent."                     => truth-1, conviction+1, flag:lied
end

@label d1_01_after
@mood calm
keeper warm "Then come in. It's cold, and I have soup, and you can lie to me tomorrow when you've slept."
narrate That is how it begins. Not with an oath — with soup.

@ach a_place
narrate End of the demo chapter.
